<http://data.silknow.org/object/d1a412e1-19cd-399d-b351-904273edb9a2/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nPURSE AND PIN CUSHIONS<br>\nBy 1680 women used fewer pins for their clothing than in 1600. As a consequence, these pin cushions are much smaller than those used earlier. Their dense, metal thread embroidery also leaves little room for pins.The display of luxury trinkets such as these in a lady's dressing room provoked contemporary writers to mock such extravagance. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d1a412e1-19cd-399d-b351-904273edb9a2> .

